quran[29]{c,v,t}:
  91,1,"By the sun and its morning brightness,"
  91,2,"and by the moon, as it follows the sun,"
  91,3,"and by the day, as it reveals the sun,"
  91,4,"and by the night, as it conceals the sun,"
  91,5,"and by the heavens and the One Who built them (as a vast universe),"
  91,6,"and by the earth and the One Who flung it far (from the sun and spread it out),"
  91,7,"and by the soul and the One Who fashioned it (in perfect proportion),"
  91,8,then inspired it with (the knowledge of) its vices and its virtues:
  91,9,"Indeed, he will succeed who purifies it,"
  91,10,"and indeed, he will fail who corrupts it."
  91,11,"The (people of) Thamud rejected (their messenger Salih) out of their rebellion,"
  91,12,when the most wicked of them rose (against him).
  91,13,Then Allah’s messenger (Salih) said to them: ‘(Do not disturb) Allah’s she-camel and her turn to drink.’
  91,14,But they denied him and slaughtered her. So their Lord crushed them for their sin and levelled their city to the ground.
  91,15,And He does not fear its consequence.
  92,1,"By the night, when it covers (everything in darkness),"
  92,2,"and by the day, when it brightens,"
  92,3,and by the One Who created the male and the female:
  92,4,"indeed, your endeavours are diverse!"
  92,5,"As for the one who gives (from his wealth) and is God-conscious,"
  92,6,"and confirms the finest promise (of the Hereafter),"
  92,7,We shall surely facilitate him towards ease (in seeking Allah’s pleasure).
  92,8,"But as for the one who is stingy and disregards (Allah’s commands for his desires),"
  92,9,"and denies the finest promise (of the Hereafter),"
  92,10,We shall surely facilitate him towards hardship (in the Hellfire).
  92,11,His wealth will not avail him when he perishes.
  92,12,"It is, indeed, upon Us to provide guidance."
  92,13,And to Us belong the latter (world) and the former (world).
  92,14,"So, I warn you of a blazing Fire,"
